1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,250
First time in Hanoi?

2
00:00:01,250 --> 00:00:03,360
Skip the tourist-trap checklist
and start here.

3
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:04,320
Number three:

4
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:05,280
Dong Xuan Market.

5
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:07,050
It is big, busy,
and has zero chill

6
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:08,360
in the best way.

7
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:09,950
Browse local snacks, fabrics,

8
00:00:09,950 --> 00:00:11,240
souvenirs, and street eats.

9
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:13,050
Pro move: go early,
carry small cash,

10
00:00:13,050 --> 00:00:14,800
and ask before taking photos.

11
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:15,560
Number two:

12
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:16,400
Hoan Kiem Lake.

13
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:18,920
It is the perfect reset
after the market chaos.

14
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:20,800
Take a slow walk,
grab an egg coffee nearby,

15
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:22,640
and watch Hanoi wake up.

16
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:23,480
Number one:

17
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:24,200
Train Street.

18
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:26,880
It is wild, iconic,
and definitely worth seeing.

19
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:29,280
But this is a real neighborhood,
not a theme park.

20
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:31,200
Follow the barriers,
listen to local security,

21
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:33,200
and never step on the tracks.

22
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:34,950
Save this for your Hanoi trip,

23
00:00:34,950 --> 00:00:36,560
and send it to your travel buddy.
